.TH HASHCHECK-RC 1 "November 2026" "Revision 3" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
hashcheck-rc \- conservative hash format detector and Hashcat wrapper
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B hashcheck-rc
.RB ( -i " HASH" " | " -f " FILE" )
.B -c CONFIG
.RB [ --mode " NUMBER" ]
.RB [ --dry-run ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Invokes Hashcat with a configured wordlist. Automatically recognizes selected structured encodings; raw hex digests require an explicit mode.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B -i HASH
Single hash value.
.TP
.B -f FILE
File containing exactly one whitespace-delimited hash.
.TP
.B -c CONFIG
JSON configuration containing hashcat_path and wordlist strings.
.TP
.B --mode NUMBER
Explicit Hashcat mode.
.TP
.B --dry-run
Show planned argument vector without launching Hashcat.
.TP
.B -h, --help
Display help.
.SH EXIT STATUS
Zero if the wrapper and Hashcat exit successfully; nonzero for invalid input or child failure. Hashcat exhaustion is not successful recovery.
.SH SECURITY
The hash is passed on the command line and may be visible in process listings.
